From 63080de577886c45019d355e21e58e3f7e69e991 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nassos Yiannopoulos <nassosyian@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:31:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 60/60] hw/display/pvg: zero-copy uploads and write-backs
 through imported guest RAM

Guest RAM is imported into Vulkan (host pointer import, 1 GiB pieces) and
the GPU works on a device-local twin of the staging arena. Uploads of
buffers and textures are GPU gathers from guest RAM recorded into a
command buffer submitted before the main one; write-backs of attachments,
compute outputs, private flushes and mip levels are GPU scatters in one
submitted after it. Ranges outside imported RAM fall back to CPU copies.
GPU writes are marked dirty. Page runs are cached per range until the
range is remapped (Map/Unmap/ReplacePhysical/task reset).

Property zero-copy (default on; off with dump-dir). Mission Control,
per 500 cmdbufs: executor 265 -> 228 ms, slowest cmdbuf 7.2 -> 4.5 ms,
CPU guest copies 99 -> 0 ms, GPU wait 102 -> 135 ms. Costs: guest RAM
stays pinned.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
